        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(google-meet): align dtmf delay default",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Google Meet plugin metadata showed a shorter `voiceCall.dtmfDelayMs` default than the runtime and docs use, which could mislead setup and config surfaces that read defaults from the manifest.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis aligns the manifest default with the existing runtime default and locks the metadata value with a manifest test. It does not touch Google Meet runtime leave-call or Chrome transport behavior.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and setup surfaces now see the same 12-second DTMF delay default that the Google Meet plugin actually applies at runtime.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/google-meet/index.test.ts extensions/google-meet/src/config.test.ts`\n- `git diff --check upstream/main..HEAD`\n- Controlled config proof: `node --import tsx - <<'EOF' ...` loaded the real Google Meet runtime config resolver and plugin manifest JSON, then compared the resolved runtime default with the manifest config-schema default.\n\n## Proof\n\n- Runtime config default: `12000`.\n- Manifest config-schema default: `12000`.\n- Controlled proof result: `aligned: true`.\n- Focused regression test covers the manifest-driven config metadata path so setup/config surfaces cannot drift back to the stale shorter default.\n",
        "branch": "llagy007/google-meet-dtmf-default-20260710",
        "head_sha": "53581da3beb6a91bd1d86688eb8e9c31e43ce139",
        "author": "llagy007",
